==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|curiusly}}, {{m|enm|curyously}}, {{m|enm|curiosly}}, {{m|enm|curiouseliche}}, {{m|enm|curyouslyche}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|curious|ly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkjɝi.əsli/|/ˈkjʊɹi.əsli/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkjʊəɹi.əsli/|/ˈkjɔːɹi.əsli/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-curiously.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{hyph|en|cu|ri|ous|ly}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[curious]] manner; with curiosity; [[inquisitive]]ly.
#: ''The children peeped '''curiously''' into the attic room.''
# [[oddly|Oddly]]; in a strange or unexpected way.
#: '''''Curiously''', when I arrived home, the front door was standing ajar.''

